 12	
 13	## Pre-Flight Fix: `GetPeerStatus` Handler
 14	
 15	### Problem
 16	`shared/bridge.ts` defines `GetPeerStatus: "getPeerStatus"`, `agent_sdk/protocol.ts` implements `getPeerStatus()`, and the webview calls `bridge.getPeerStatus()`. But **no handler exists** in `src/handlers/` to route this to the CLI.
 17	
 18	### Fix
 19	
 20	#### `src/handlers/session.handler.ts` (or new `src/handlers/peer.handler.ts`)
 21	
 22	```typescript
 23	[Methods.GetPeerStatus]: async (_params, ctx): Promise<{
 24	  think: PeerStatus | null;
 25	  do: PeerStatus | null;
 26	}> => {
 27	  const metaSession = ctx.getMetaSession?.();
 28	  if (!metaSession) {
 29	    return { think: null, do: null };
 30	  }
 31	
 32	  // Query Think session
 33	  let thinkStatus: PeerStatus | null = null;
 34	  try {
 35	    thinkStatus = await metaSession.think.getPeerStatus?.() || null;
 36	  } catch {
 37	    // ignore
 38	  }
 39	
 40	  // Query Do session
 41	  let doStatus: PeerStatus | null = null;
 42	  try {
 43	    doStatus = await metaSession.do.getPeerStatus?.() || null;
 44	  } catch {
 45	    // ignore
 46	  }
 47	
 48	  return { think: thinkStatus, do: doStatus };
 49	},
 50	```
 51	
 52	**Note:** `Session.getPeerStatus()` may need to be added to the `Session` interface in `agent_sdk/session.ts` if not already present. It should call `this.client.getPeerStatus()`.
