 56	## Sub-Phase 7.1: Session Persistence on Reload
 57	
 58	### Problem
 59	On VS Code: window reload, `BridgeHandler` is recreated with an empty `metaSessions` map. The webview starts fresh.
 60	
 61	### Solution
 62	Persist `thinkSessionId`, `doSessionId`, `workDir`, `model`, `thinking` in `workspaceState`. On webview setup, auto-restore if data exists and session directories still exist on disk. **MVP = reconnect session IDs only** (no history replay).
 63	
 64	### Files
 65	
 66	#### `src/bridge-handler.ts`
 67	
 68	Add persistence helpers:
 69	
 70	```typescript
 71	interface PersistedMetaSession {
 72	  thinkSessionId: string;
 73	  doSessionId: string;
 74	  workDir: string;
 75	  model: string;
 76	  thinking: boolean;
 77	  timestamp: number;
 78	}
 79	
 80	private persistKey(webviewId: string): string {
 81	  return `metaSession:${webviewId}`;
 82	}
 83	
 84	async persistMetaSession(webviewId: string, metaSession: MetaSession): Promise<void> {
 85	  const payload: PersistedMetaSession = {
 86	    thinkSessionId: metaSession.think.sessionId,
 87	    doSessionId: metaSession.do.sessionId,
 88	    workDir: metaSession.workDir,
 89	    model: metaSession.think.model || "",
 90	    thinking: metaSession.think.thinking,
 91	    timestamp: Date.now(),
 92	  };
 93	  await this.workspaceState.update(this.persistKey(webviewId), payload);
 94	}
 95	
 96	getPersistedMetaSession(webviewId: string): PersistedMetaSession | undefined {
 97	  return this.workspaceState.get<PersistedMetaSession>(this.persistKey(webviewId));
 98	}
 99	
100	async clearPersistedMetaSession(webviewId: string): Promise<void> {
101	  await this.workspaceState.update(this.persistKey(webviewId), undefined);
102	}
103	```
104	
105	Call `persistMetaSession` after creating a meta-session. Call `clearPersistedMetaSession` in `disposeView` and `closeMetaSession`.
106	
107	Add helper to check if session directory exists:
108	
109	```typescript
110	import { existsSync } from "fs";
111	import path from "path";
112	
113	function sessionDirExists(workDir: string, sessionId: string): boolean {
114	  // Use KimiPaths or construct directly
115	  const sessionsDir = path.join(workDir, ".kimi", "sessions", sessionId);
116	  return existsSync(sessionsDir);
117	}
118	```
119	
120	#### `src/bridge-handler.ts` — Auto-restore on setup
121	
122	In `createContext` or `getOrCreateMetaSession`, check for persisted data:
123	
124	```typescript
125	async getOrCreateMetaSession(
126	  webviewId: string,
127	  model: string,
128	  thinking: boolean,
129	  thinkSessionId?: string,
130	  doSessionId?: string,
131	): Promise<MetaSession> {
132	  // If caller didn't provide IDs, check for persisted ones
133	  if (!thinkSessionId || !doSessionId) {
134	    const persisted = this.getPersistedMetaSession(webviewId);
135	    if (persisted) {
136	      const thinkExists = sessionDirExists(persisted.workDir, persisted.thinkSessionId);
137	      const doExists = sessionDirExists(persisted.workDir, persisted.doSessionId);
138	
139	      if (thinkExists || doExists) {
140	        thinkSessionId = thinkExists ? persisted.thinkSessionId : undefined;
141	        doSessionId = doExists ? persisted.doSessionId : undefined;
142	        // Use persisted model/thinking if current params are defaults
143	        if (!model && persisted.model) model = persisted.model;
144	      } else {
145	        // Sessions deleted — clean up
146	        await this.clearPersistedMetaSession(webviewId);
147	      }
148	    }
149	  }
150	
151	  // ... rest of existing logic ...
152	}
153	```
154	
155	#### `src/KimiWebviewProvider.ts` — Broadcast restore event
156	
157	After setting up a webview, if a meta-session was restored, broadcast a `RestoredSession` event:
158	
159	```typescript
160	private async setupWebview(webviewId: string, webview: vscode.Webview): Promise<void> {
161	  // ... existing setup ...
162	
163	  const metaSession = this.bridgeHandler.getMetaSession(webviewId);
164	  if (metaSession) {
165	    this.broadcastInternal("RestoredSession", {
166	      thinkSessionId: metaSession.think.sessionId,
167	      doSessionId: metaSession.do.sessionId,
168	    }, webviewId);
169	  }
170	}
171	```
172	
173	#### `webview-ui/src/App.tsx` or `hooks/useAppInit.ts`
174	
175	Listen for `RestoredSession` and reconnect:
176	
177	```typescript
178	useEffect(() => {
179	  const unsub = bridge.on(Events.RestoredSession, (payload: {
180	    thinkSessionId: string;
181	    doSessionId: string;
182	  }) => {
183	    // Reconnect sessions (no history replay for MVP)
184	    loadSession("think", payload.thinkSessionId, []);
185	    loadSession("do", payload.doSessionId, []);
186	    toast.info("Previous session restored");
187	  });
188	  return () => unsub();
189	}, [loadSession]);
190	```
191	
192	**Note:** `loadSession` with empty events `[]` sets `sessionId` but leaves `messages` empty. This is the **MVP** — the user can continue the session but doesn't see old messages. Full history replay would require fetching wire logs, which is a larger feature.
193	
194	### Acceptance Criteria
195	- [x] Creating a meta-session writes persisted state to `workspaceState`
196	- [x] Closing a webview clears persisted state
197	- [x] Reloading VS Code: auto-restores session IDs if directories still exist
198	- [x] If session directories were deleted, persisted state is cleaned up
199	- [x] Restored sessions reconnect without manual user action
200	- [x] Toast notification confirms restore
