346	## Sub-Phase 7.4: Approval Routing Optimization
347	
348	### Problem
349	`respondApproval` sends to both Think and Do turns.
350	
351	### Solution (simpler than original plan): Store `tab` in the webview's approval request.
352	
353	### Files
354	
355	#### `webview-ui/src/stores/approval.store.ts`
356	
357	Add `tab` to `ApprovalRequest`:
358	
359	```typescript
360	export interface ApprovalRequest {
361	  id: string;
362	  tool_call_id: string;
363	  sender: string;
364	  action: string;
365	  description: string;
366	  display: DisplayBlock[];
367	  tab: "think" | "do"; // NEW
368	}
369	```
370	
371	#### `webview-ui/src/stores/event-handlers.ts`
372	
373	Pass `tab` when adding request:
374	
375	```typescript
376	ApprovalRequest: (draft, payload: ApprovalRequestPayload) => {
377	  const tab = draft.sessionId === payload.session_id ? "think" : "do";
378	  useApprovalStore.getState().addRequest({ ...payload, tab });
379	},
380	```
381	
382	**Wait** — `ApprovalRequest` handler receives the payload but not the draft context in the current architecture. The `ApprovalRequest` event comes from the wire stream and is processed by `processEventForTab`. The draft is a `TabState`, so we can infer the tab from which `processEventForTab` was called. But `useApprovalStore` is global.
383	
384	**Better approach:** The event handler for `ApprovalRequest` runs within `processEventForTab`, so it knows the tab. Store the tab in the approval request:
385	
386	```typescript
387	// In event-handlers.ts
388	ApprovalRequest: (draft: TabState, payload: ApprovalRequestPayload) => {
389	  const tab = draft.sessionId ? (/* figure out tab */) : "think";
390	  // Actually, processEventForTab knows the tab via the draft param
391	  // But we need to pass it to the approval store
392	},
393	```
394	
395	Actually, `processEventForTab` receives a `TabState` draft, not the tab name. We need to know whether this is Think or Do tab. Options:
396	
397	1. Pass tab name into `processEventForTab`: `processEventForTab(draft, event, tab)`
398	2. Infer from `_sessionId` in the event (already done in `processEvent`)
399	
400	**Recommended:** Add `tab` parameter to `processEventForTab`:
401	
402	```typescript
403	// In chat.store.ts processEvent:
404	processEventForTab(draft.think, event, "think");
405	processEventForTab(draft.do, event, "do");
406	
407	// In event-handlers.ts:
408	const eventHandlers: Record<string, (draft: TabState, payload: any, tab: "think" | "do") => void> = {
409	  ApprovalRequest: (draft, payload, tab) => {
410	    useApprovalStore.getState().addRequest({ ...payload, tab });
411	  },
412	};
413	```
414	
415	#### `webview-ui/src/stores/approval.store.ts`
416	
417	```typescript
418	respondToRequest: async (id, response) => {
419	  const req = get().pending.find((r) => r.id === id);
420	  if (!req) return;
421	  await bridge.respondApproval(id, response, req.tab);
422	  get().removeRequest(id);
423	},
424	```
425	
426	#### `webview-ui/src/services/bridge.ts`
427	
428	```typescript
429	respondApproval(requestId: string, response: ApprovalResponse, tab?: "think" | "do") {
430	  return this.call<{ ok: boolean }>(Methods.RespondApproval, { requestId, response, tab });
431	}
432	```
433	
434	#### `src/handlers/chat.handler.ts`
435	
436	```typescript
437	[Methods.RespondApproval]: async (params: { requestId: string; response: ApprovalResponse; tab?: "think" | "do" }, ctx) => {
438	  const tab = params.tab || "think";
439	  const turn = tab === "think" ? ctx.getThinkTurn() : ctx.getDoTurn();
440	  if (!turn) return { ok: false };
441	  await turn.approve(params.requestId, params.response);
442	  return { ok: true };
443	},
444	```
445	
446	### Acceptance Criteria
447	- [x] Approval responses route to the exact session that emitted the request
448	- [x] No fallback "try both" behavior in normal operation
449	- [x] Falls back to "think" if tab is missing (backward compat)
