453	## Sub-Phase 7.5: Meta-Session Rename & Pairing
454	
455	### Problem
456	Think and Do sessions are created independently with no persistent link. The extension's `MetaSession` is in-memory only. `SessionList` shows flat sessions with no indication of which Think/Do sessions belong together.
457	
458	### Solution
459	**Minimal viable approach:** Reuse the existing `metadata.json` per-session file to store `pairedSessionId` and `mode`. No new storage layer. No grouped UI refactor. Just mode badges, auto-pair loading, and cascade rename/delete.
460	
461	### CLI Prerequisite (small change)
462	
463	#### `src/consilium/session_state.py`
464	
465	Add one field to `SessionState`:
466	
467	```python
468	class SessionState(BaseModel):
469	    # ... existing fields ...
470	    todos: list[TodoItemState] = Field(default_factory=list)
471	    paired_session_id: str | None = None  # NEW
472	```
473	
474	Because `SessionState` uses Pydantic `model_validate()`, old files without this field default to `None`. No migration needed.
475	
476	#### `src/consilium/plan/models.py`
477	
478	Add `think_session_id` to `Dispatch`:
479	
480	```python
481	class Dispatch(BaseModel):
482	    # ... existing fields ...
483	    afk_mode: bool = False
484	    think_session_id: str | None = None  # NEW
485	```
486	
487	#### `src/consilium/plan/dispatch.py`
488	
489	Accept `think_session_id` in `write_dispatch()` and include it.
490	
491	#### `src/consilium/think/push.py` and `think/slash.py`
492	
493	Pass the Think session ID into `push_plan_to_do()` so it gets written into the dispatch.
494	
495	#### `src/consilium/app.py`
496	
497	When creating a Do session, read `dispatch.json`. If it contains `think_session_id`, set the Do session's `state.paired_session_id` and save.
